      "explanation": "Expanding only as far as \\(9!\\) reveals a common factor: \\(11!=11\\cdot10\\cdot9!\\) and \\(10!=10\\cdot9!\\). Since \\(9!>0\\), we may cancel it to obtain\n\\[\n\\frac{11!-10!}{9!}\n=\\frac{(110-10)9!}{9!}\n=100.\n\\]\nThus the value is \\(100\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
